From 264f1e1b42b179cb6e49c90c3b71facf1ffddab7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sean Dougherty <sdougherty@microsoft.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 22:39:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] erofs: isolate dm-verity devices by SELinux mount context

SELinux mount labels belong to filesystem superblocks. Reusing one verity mapper across distinct mount contexts therefore fails when the kernel reuses that superblock. Include explicit SELinux mount options in mapper identity for both signed and unsigned layers, retaining existing names for unlabeled mounts and all signature verification checks.

Add identity tests and a privileged regression mounting one layer concurrently without a context and with two allocated MCS labels.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
